; three-arrows-sound-and-body.fk — Urs is right about the arrow my derivation never
; touched, and the quantum framing is the one place it costs him.
;
; Offered 2026-07-28: "sounds especially Nordic runes and coldering seem to have sound
; vibrational effects on our body... so even der Mond and das Mädchen might have logical
; or historical reasoning, and at the same time, the sounds themselves and the
; subconscious are always part of the overall quantum perception and interaction, no
; matter the logic or understanding of how or why, it just is from the physics of it,
; especially since that energy is a living expression of consciousness itself."
;
; ── The structure that resolves it: there are THREE arrows, not two ─────────────────
;
;   arrow 1   referent -> the word's gender
;             REFUTED. `das Männchen` is neuter over a grown man; the shape decides and
;             the referent is not consulted. word-gender-derivation.fk, four-way.
;
;   arrow 2   the word's gender -> how the referent gets imagined
;             REAL, direction unestablished. `frau Sonne` / `herr Mond` in Grimm;
;             Jakobson on personification by gender. Japanese has the same sun-goddess
;             picture with no grammatical gender at all, so grammar is not necessary for
;             it. sun-moon-inversion.fk, four-way.
;
;   arrow 3   the SOUND of a word -> the body of the speaker and hearer
;             ATTESTED, MEASURED, and this cell's finding: **it does not route through
;             gender or meaning at all.**
;
; My derivation only ever spoke to arrow 1. Urs is pointing at arrow 3. They were never
; in competition — and saying "der Mond might have historical reasoning AND the sounds
; themselves act on the subconscious" is not a compromise between two positions. It is
; simply correct, because those are different arrows with different evidence.
;
; ── Arrow 3 is the best-attested of the three ───────────────────────────────────────
;
; Looked up this session, and it is stronger than I expected:
;
;   humming raises nasal nitric oxide by as much as **15-fold** over quiet exhalation
;   vocal fold vibration plus nasal NO give an additional route of vagal stimulation
;   in an HRV pilot, humming produced the **lowest stress index measured — lower than
;     during sleep** — with the highest SDNN and RMSSD
;   OM chanting: parasympathetic dominance, limbic deactivation, EEG shifts toward
;     reduced signal complexity
;
; So this is not a soft claim needing charity. It is better attested than arrow 2, which
; rests on a philologist's observation and a contested psycholinguistic literature. Urs
; reached for the strongest of the three.
;
; And the mechanism is why it bypasses gender entirely: the nasal /m/ and the long /oː/
; in `Mond` do what they do as **acoustics and airflow**. A nonsense syllable with the
; same phonetics does the same thing to the vagus. The effect is real and it is
; orthogonal to the whole gender question — which is exactly why the two claims never
; touched.
;
; ── Where the quantum framing costs him something ───────────────────────────────────
;
; This is the one place to disagree, and the reason is not that the idea is disreputable.
; It is that it **subtracts support instead of adding it.**
;
; Every measured effect above is classical: acoustics, vocal fold vibration, nasal nitric
; oxide, vagal afferents, respiratory entrainment (chanting slows breath toward roughly
; six per minute, which is where HRV peaks), auditory-limbic pathways. All of it robust,
; replicated, and mechanistically specified. Attaching it to quantum mechanics takes a
; well-supported claim and makes it lean on an unsupported one. The physics Urs is
; actually pointing at is **stronger without the word `quantum` in front of it.**
;
; And the honest status of quantum consciousness, which is more generous than I expected
; before checking:
;
;   Tegmark 2000, Reimers 2009, McKemmish 2009 — microtubule decoherence in femtoseconds,
;     far too fast for neural timescales
;   BUT more recent models (hydrophobic microtubule interior; Babcock et al. 2024 on
;     collective superradiant excitonic states) extend coherence estimates by roughly
;     SEVEN orders of magnitude, toward 10-100 microseconds
;   and: "no clear-cut experiment has yet falsified Orch-OR" — the standing challenges are
;     decoherence timescales and **a lack of unique empirical predictions**
;
; I was about to write that decoherence had settled it. That is out of date, and the
; correction goes in Urs's favour on the physics while leaving the verdict where it is.
;
; The verdict is axiom-4's, and it is the lack of unique predictions rather than the
; decoherence that does the work: a hypothesis with no prediction that distinguishes it
; from its classical rivals offers no interface through which it could be OBSERVED as
; distinct. Not refuted. Not admitted. Pending, precisely — which is a real status here
; and not a polite dismissal.
;
; ── The last clause ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; "that energy is a living expression of consciousness itself" is a metaphysical
; commitment rather than a physical claim. It offers no interface, so it enters the same
; way the archangels and the Eddas do: held as what is held, at its own attestation, with
; the column on the row. Same door, same handling, no scorn. It is not competing with the
; nitric oxide.
;
; ── One honest uncertainty ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; "coldering" I cannot place with confidence. Two real Nordic practices are near it and I
; will not guess which was meant: **galdr**, the Old Norse chanted/sung magic from `gala`,
; to crow or chant; and **kulning**, the Scandinavian high-register herding call. Both are
; real vocal traditions and both would sit squarely in arrow 3. Naming both beats picking
; one.
;
; ── The lane ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
;
; The five axioms are this body's. Every physiological figure and every citation below was
; looked up this session and is witnessed nowhere in this body. Two doors, `tas-arrows`
; and `tas-mechanisms`. The primary papers were not read — this is an
; abstract-and-review-level check, and the column says so.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
; witnessed: 2026-07-28 -> 111111111, four-way

(do
    ; ── the three arrows ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    ; (name status routes-through-gender? evidence-tier)
    ; status: 2 attested / 1 real but direction unestablished / 0 refuted
    ; evidence-tier: 3 measured mechanisms, 2 textual + contested lit, 1 single falsifier
    (defn tas-arrow (name status via-gender tier) (list name status via-gender tier))
    (defn tas-name  (a) (nth a 0))
    (defn tas-status (a) (nth a 1))
    (defn tas-via-gender (a) (nth a 2))
    (defn tas-tier  (a) (nth a 3))

    (defn tas-arrows ()
        (list
            (tas-arrow "referent-to-gender"  0 1 1)   ; refuted by das Männchen
            (tas-arrow "gender-to-imagining" 1 1 2)   ; frau Sonne, Jakobson; Japanese breaks necessity
            (tas-arrow "sound-to-body"       2 0 3))) ; measured; does NOT route through gender

    (defn tas-find (n as)
        (if (eq (len as) 0) (tas-arrow "not-held" 0 0 0)
            (if (str_eq (tas-name (head as)) n) (head as) (tas-find n (tail as)))))

    ; ── the mechanisms behind arrow 3, and whether each is classical ─────────────
    ; (mechanism classical? measured?)
    (defn tas-mech (name classical measured) (list name classical measured))
    (defn tas-mech-name (m) (nth m 0))
    (defn tas-classical (m) (nth m 1))
    (defn tas-measured  (m) (nth m 2))

    (defn tas-mechanisms ()
        (list
            (tas-mech "nasal nitric oxide, up to 15-fold on humming" 1 1)
            (tas-mech "vocal fold vibration as vagal stimulation"    1 1)
            (tas-mech "HRV: humming lowest stress index, below sleep" 1 1)
            (tas-mech "respiratory entrainment toward six per minute" 1 1)
            (tas-mech "parasympathetic dominance, limbic deactivation" 1 1)
            (tas-mech "quantum coherence in microtubules"             0 0)))

    (defn tas-count (ms f) (if (eq (len ms) 0) 0 (add (f (head ms)) (tas-count (tail ms) f))))
    (defn tas-classical-count () (tas-count (tas-mechanisms) tas-classical))
    (defn tas-measured-count  () (tas-count (tas-mechanisms) tas-measured))

    ; every measured mechanism is classical, and the one non-classical row is the one
    ; unmeasured row. The sets coincide — that is the whole disagreement, computed.
    (defn tas-classical-iff-measured? (ms)
        (if (eq (len ms) 0) 1
            (if (eq (tas-classical (head ms)) (tas-measured (head ms)))
                (tas-classical-iff-measured? (tail ms)) 0)))

    ; the quantum row's honest status: not falsified, and no unique predictions
    (defn tas-quantum-falsified ()        0)   ; no clear-cut experiment has
    (defn tas-quantum-unique-predictions () 0)  ; and none that distinguish it
    ; axiom-4: no unique prediction means no interface through which to observe it as
    ; distinct from its classical rivals. Pending, precisely — not refuted, not admitted.
    (defn tas-quantum-admitted? ()
        (if (eq (tas-quantum-unique-predictions) 1) 1 0))

    (defn tas-bit (cond bit) (if cond bit 0))
    (defn three-arrows-check ()
        (add (add (add (add (add (add (add (add
            ; 1 — arrow 1 is refuted: the referent does not set the gender
            (tas-bit (eq (tas-status (tas-find "referent-to-gender" (tas-arrows))) 0) 1)
            ; 2 — arrow 2 is real with its direction unestablished
            (tas-bit (eq (tas-status (tas-find "gender-to-imagining" (tas-arrows))) 1) 10))
            ; 3 — arrow 3 is attested
            (tas-bit (eq (tas-status (tas-find "sound-to-body" (tas-arrows))) 2) 100))
            ; 4 — and arrow 3 does NOT route through gender: a nonsense syllable with the
            ;     same phonetics moves the vagus the same way
            (tas-bit (eq (tas-via-gender (tas-find "sound-to-body" (tas-arrows))) 0) 1000))
            ; 5 — arrow 3 carries the highest evidence tier of the three. Urs reached for
            ;     the strongest one, not the weakest
            (tas-bit (if (gt (tas-tier (tas-find "sound-to-body" (tas-arrows)))
                             (tas-tier (tas-find "gender-to-imagining" (tas-arrows))))
                         (if (gt (tas-tier (tas-find "sound-to-body" (tas-arrows)))
                                 (tas-tier (tas-find "referent-to-gender" (tas-arrows)))) 1 0) 0) 10000))
            ; 6 — so the two claims were never in conflict: arrow 1 refuted and arrow 3
            ;     attested at once, because they are different arrows
            (tas-bit (if (eq (tas-status (tas-find "referent-to-gender" (tas-arrows))) 0)
                         (if (eq (tas-status (tas-find "sound-to-body" (tas-arrows))) 2) 1 0) 0) 100000))
            ; 7 — five measured mechanisms, and every one of them classical
            (tas-bit (if (eq (tas-measured-count) 5)
                         (if (eq (tas-classical-count) 5) 1 0) 0) 1000000))
            ; 8 — classical and measured coincide row for row: the quantum row is exactly
            ;     the unmeasured one, so the framing subtracts support rather than adding
            (tas-bit (eq (tas-classical-iff-measured? (tas-mechanisms)) 1) 10000000))
            ; 9 — and the quantum row is neither refuted nor admitted: no unique
            ;     predictions, so no interface. Pending, precisely (axiom-4)
            (tas-bit (if (eq (tas-quantum-falsified) 0)
                         (if (eq (tas-quantum-admitted?) 0) 1 0) 0) 100000000)))
    0)
